## 2. 50 MB through the app server versus presigned
   concept: a proxied upload costs the app a socket, CPU for every byte and, if it buffers, the whole file in memory; a presigned upload costs it one signature
   [storage] PUT /member-documents/proxied/buffer-f0388403-2165-421a-822f-18b4c72598a9?<presigned> (client, query) -> 200 52428800 bytes in
   ok   proxied (buffer) 50 MB upload stored (201)
   [storage] PUT /member-documents/proxied/stream-0781ad1d-0ea0-46a9-b07d-3c79f5d4a76f?<presigned> (client, query) -> 200 52428800 bytes in
   ok   proxied (stream) 50 MB upload stored (201)
   [storage] PUT /member-documents/quarantine/1498f199-2a90-4f07-8cf2-740722fb3f39?<presigned> (client, query) -> 200 52428800 bytes in
   [storage] HEAD /member-documents/quarantine/1498f199-2a90-4f07-8cf2-740722fb3f39 (sdk, header) -> 200
   ok   presigned 50 MB upload stored (200) and confirmed (uploaded)
   mode        wall ms   app bytes read   app CPU ms   app peak memory +MB
   buffer          791         52428800          411              150.6
   stream          939         52428800          297               16.6
   presigned       994               81           26                  1
   ok   buffering holds the whole file: the app's peak live memory grows by more than 40 MB
   ok   streaming keeps memory flat (under 25 MB) but the app still reads all 52,428,800 bytes
   ok   presigned: the app reads under 1 KB, and uses under a fifth of the CPU of the cheaper proxied upload

## 3. What a presigned URL allows, and what it does not
   concept: the signature covers method, bucket, key, expiry and the signed headers (content-type, content-length, host); change one and storage computes a different signature
   app, text/html: 400 type text/html is not accepted (allowed: application/pdf, image/png, image/jpeg, text/plain)
   app, 200 MB: 400 size must be 1..104857600 bytes
   ok   the app refuses to sign a type outside the allow-list or a size over 100 MB
   [storage] HEAD /member-documents/quarantine/57b6d247-7ab6-4965-b4c0-fa4492eb6d50 (sdk, header) -> 404
   complete before any PUT: 409 object not found in storage: upload it first
   ok   the app does not take the browser's word: completing before uploading is refused after a HEAD
